wine (10.0.1-4cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add runtime dependencies on libxrandr2 and libxrender1 (both amd64 and
    i386) so the built-in XRandR display handler can load in 32-bit Wine.
  * Add 0008-xvidmode-switch-sync-assert.patch: guard XF86VidMode mode
    switches when the private mode pointer is missing and force an XSync
    so asynchronous BadValue errors are caught instead of killing the
    calling process.
  * Add 0009-xrandr-notify-desktop-on-mode-change.patch: notify the shell
    and broadcast WM_DISPLAYCHANGE to all top-level windows on mode switch,
    so the desktop window and the ReactOS Explorer taskbar reposition after
    a resolution change. Self-initiated switches (desk.cpl) only refresh the
    driver state under the win32u display devices lock and are notified
    after it is released, avoiding a self-deadlock on the non-recursive
    display_lock mutex, and the broadcast is non-blocking so a mode switch
    no longer stalls for 2s per top-level window.

 -- Artem <artem@example.com>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:20:00 +0300

wine (10.0.1-3cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add 0005-gdifont-default-gui-size.patch: stock DEFAULT_GUI_FONT
    -11/-12 -> -14 px for all charsets, so shell surfaces that never
    set an explicit font (start menu band, taskbar buttons, tray clock)
    match the global UI font size.
  * Add 0006-dialog-font-scale.patch: scale dialog template fonts by
    5/4 (8 pt -> 14 px); the whole dialog scales proportionally with
    the text, since base units are measured from the created font.
  * Add 0007-uxtheme-button-dc-font.patch: GetThemeFont resolves the
    label font from the DC only for the Button/PUSHBUTTON part, so
    dialog push button text follows the dialog font while the theme
    keeps drawing everything and every other class/part keeps the
    theme font.
  * Dockerfile: move apt-get update into the build-dep layer so the
    package index refreshes whenever the source tree changes.

 -- Artem <artem@example.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0300

